{#
    The gift card panel in the checkout sidebar, directly under the totals.

    That is the moment the customer is looking at what they are about to pay, so it is where they
    look for a way to pay less of it. Before this the panel existed only on the cart page, and a
    customer already in checkout had to go back to find it.

    The sidebar is a separate hook region from the step's own form, so this form is not nested
    inside another one - see config/twig_hooks/shop.yaml.
#}
{% set order = hookable_metadata.context.order|default(null) %}

{#
    Where the controller should send the customer back to. Mapped from the current route rather than
    submitted as a URL: the apply endpoint is reachable anonymously, and one that redirects wherever
    it is told is an open redirect. The controller accepts only these keys and falls back to the
    cart, so a forged value achieves nothing.
#}
{% set return_to = {
    'sylius_shop_checkout_address': 'checkout_address',
    'sylius_shop_checkout_select_shipping': 'checkout_shipping',
    'sylius_shop_checkout_select_payment': 'checkout_payment',
    'sylius_shop_checkout_complete': 'checkout_complete',
}[app.request.attributes.get('_route')]|default('cart') %}

{% if order is not null and not order.empty %}
    <div class="mt-4 pt-3 border-top" {{ sylius_test_html_attribute('checkout-gift-card-panel') }}>
        <h6 class="mb-3">{{ 'madcoders_sylius_gift_card.ui.gift_cards'|trans }}</h6>

        {% include '@MadcodersSyliusGiftCardPlugin/shop/common/gift_card_panel.html.twig' with {
            'order': order,
            'return_to': return_to,
            'compact': true,
        } only %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
